ARCHITECT SPEC: ListNinja (Chrome Extension MV3)
Core Philosophy: A browser-native workflow engine for high-leverage data capture. Not a "to-do" app, but a productivity repository.

1. TECH STACK & ARCHITECTURE
Framework: React + Vite (Fast HMR, component-based state).

Styling: Tailwind CSS (Custom Glassmorphism utilities).

Icons: Lucide React (Mapped to specific list types).

Storage: - chrome.storage.local: Primary data store for all Lists (bypasses 100KB sync limit).

chrome.storage.sync: User preferences (Themes, Settings).

2. DYNAMIC CONTEXT MENU (THE "HOOK")
Behavior: Right-click highlighted text -> "Save to ListNinja" -> [Dynamic Submenu of existing lists] + "Create New List".

Background Logic: background.js must use chrome.contextMenus.removeAll() and create() inside a chrome.storage.onChanged listener to keep the menu synced with the sidebar.

Data Payload: Capture selectionText, pageUrl, pageTitle, and timestamp.

New List Flow: Use chrome.action.openPopup() to trigger the UI with the captured text in a "Pending" state for naming.

3. UI: THE GLASSMORPHIC WORKSPACE
Sidebar (Left): Collapsible. Displays List names + type-specific icons.

Workspace (Right): The active list. Header includes:

List Title (Editable).

Global Toggle: Enable/Disable checkboxes or bullets regardless of type.

Download Button: Export current list to .txt or .csv.

Themes (Toggle in Settings):

Light: Frosted white glass (rgba(255,255,255,0.2)), high-contrast dark text.

Medium (Default): Smoked grey/blue glass (rgba(40,40,50,0.4)), 12px blur.

Dark: Deep obsidian glass (rgba(0,0,0,0.7)), low transparency, light grey text.

4. LIST TYPES & FORMATTING
Blank (Default): Plain text area.

To-Do: List items with functional checkboxes.

Clipboard: Bulleted list format with a "Copy All to Clipboard" button.

Note: CSS-ruled notebook paper background.

Gym Log: - Structure: Two-column CSS Grid (Exercise | Sets/Weight).

Icon: Dumbbell.

Logic: "Add Row" button at the bottom.

5. DATA PORTABILITY (HUMAN-CENTRIC EXPORTS)
The "Machine" Backup (.json): Single button in Settings to export/import the entire app state for backups.

The "Human" Download (.txt): Available for all text-based lists. Formats checkboxes as [ ] and appends Source URLs as footnotes.

The "Data" Download (.csv): Exclusive to Gym Logs.

Columns: Date, Exercise, Sets/Weight, Source.

Logic: Sanitize commas in user input to prevent Excel formatting errors.

6. ENGINEERING CONSTRAINTS
Zero Framework Bloat: Use standard React hooks (useState, useEffect, useMemo).

MV3 Compliance: No eval(), no external scripts. Everything bundled via Vite.

Persistence: High-frequency auto-save to chrome.storage.local.
